Answer:
Since you mentioned you're looking for an efficient algorithm, and assuming you get the dictionary in advance (and not just as a callable predicate), you can use the AhoâCorasick algorithm.

Of course, if the input text is short, a more naive algorithm will be faster, for avoiding the "expensive" pre-processing of the dictionary.

Plus, an alternative python-answer: here's a simple way to simply check each substring:

def gen_words(txt):
    n = len(txt)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i+1, n+1):
            subtxt = txt[i:j]
            if is_word(subtxt):
                yield subtxt


For uniqueness, do:

all_words = set(gen_words(txt))

